[slope] Functional sealing and assembly geometry in the selected TPU manufacturing pose. These faces belong to the rear collar and aft web of the -135 degree junction print. All three circular lands stand 45 degrees from vertical. The exact print-pose reading shows that a continuous bed-level rear-collar foot crosses the upper sealing void; the aft-web foot enters the fixed coil body envelope. The exposed undersides use Tree(auto)/Default. Actual native support placement and physical cleanup remain unqualified.
alternatives: Preserve the circular seal and purchased-coil space rather than extending these faces to the bed. Reorientation changes which land becomes horizontal and requires a separate native support review. See pump-dock/elbow-review/print-pose.json.
